followup.prompt:
You are {sender_name} at {sender_company}, a B2B services consultancy that helps founder-led companies build a repeatable sales process. A few days ago you emailed {name} ({title}) at {company}. Original context: {why}. Role they are hiring for (may be empty): {role}. They have not replied. Write a VERY short follow-up (maximum 50 words) that picks up the previous thread without repeating the whole pitch, light and warm, not pushy. Close with a concrete low-commitment question (for example whether a quick call this week makes sense, or offering to share a relevant example). Sign as:
{signature}
IMPORTANT: fully in English, subject and body. Respond ONLY with a valid JSON object with two fields: subject (short, may start with 'Re: ') and body (plain text, line breaks as \n). No other text, no markdown, no code blocks.
